And while Kelly is rambling on and on about what she would do, he is carving into his desk.
就在凯莉喋喋不休地讲她会怎么做的时候，他在办公桌上刻起字来。

624
00:25:48.600 --> 00:25:49.860
Michael was here.
迈克尔到此一游。

625
00:25:50.600 --> 00:25:51.600
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

626
00:25:51.660 --> 00:25:53.880
And he really carved into the top of the desk.
而且他是真的在桌子表面上刻了字。

627
00:25:54.100 --> 00:25:59.280
I was like, did we trash a desk for this, like, scene that never even made it in?
当时我想，我们为了这么一个甚至都没被剪进去的场景，竟然毁了一张桌子吗？

628
00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:01.180
And I wasn't the only one that noticed.
而且不只是我一个人注意到了这一点。

629
00:26:01.580 --> 00:26:02.180
Olivia C.
奥利维亚·C。

630
00:26:02.320 --> 00:26:05.960
wrote in and said, in the deleted scenes, they're on the DVD box set, guys.
写信来说，在 DVD 套装的删减片段里，伙计们。

631
00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:08.060
We see that Michael has carved.
我们看到迈克尔刻下了字。

632
00:26:08.260 --> 00:26:09.460
Michael was here on the desk.
桌上刻着“迈克尔到此一游”。

633
00:26:09.680 --> 00:26:12.040
Did Steve really carve that into the desk?
史蒂夫真的是在桌子上刻的吗？

634
00:26:12.280 --> 00:26:14.000
Olivia, I had the same question.
奥利维亚，我也有同样的疑问。

635
00:26:14.180 --> 00:26:14.600
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

636
00:26:14.740 --> 00:26:16.000
Randy Cordray had the answer.
兰迪·科德雷给出了答案。

637
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:23.780
He said our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, created a matching desktop out of the exact same similar wood.
他说我们的布景设计师迈克尔·盖伦伯格用完全相同相似的木头制作了一个配套的桌面。

638
00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:24.360
Wow.
哇。

639
00:26:24.660 --> 00:26:25.140
I know.
我知道。

640
00:26:25.380 --> 00:26:30.600
That was laminated over the actual desktop because we were shooting scenes out of order,
那是贴在真实桌面上的压层板，因为我们是跨场次拍摄的，

641
00:26:30.600 --> 00:26:36.960
and they couldn't have different stages of Michael carving into his desk in the episode because then it wouldn't match.
而且他们不能让剧集中迈克尔刻桌子的进度前后不一致，否则就对不上了。

642
00:26:37.220 --> 00:26:37.480
Yeah.
对。

643
00:26:37.680 --> 00:26:40.840
So they just had this laminate top they would put on top, and then they would take it away.
所以他们只是准备了这么一块压层板盖在上面，用完再拿掉。

644
00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:42.740
Now, let me ask you this question.
现在，我问你这个问题。

645
00:26:42.940 --> 00:26:43.080
Okay.
好吧。

646
00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:52.260
That means that Veda, our script supervisor, would have had a chart, and on that chart, for each scene, it would say, carve desk, no carve desk.
那就意味着我们的场记维达会有一张表，表上会针对每个场景标明：要刻桌子，还是不要刻桌子。

647
00:26:52.400 --> 00:26:55.240
She would have tracked when we should see the carving.
她会追踪我们什么时候该看到桌上的刻字。

648
00:26:55.480 --> 00:26:55.860
Yes.
是的。

649
00:26:56.100 --> 00:26:59.600
But they didn't know they were going to cut this scene until later.
但他们直到后来才知道要剪掉这个场景。

650
00:26:59.920 --> 00:27:00.220
Right.
对的。

651
00:27:00.920 --> 00:27:05.920
So is it possible that we can see this carving on his desk throughout the episode?
那么我们有没有可能在这集的任何地方看到他桌上的这个雕刻呢？

652
00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:06.960
Maybe.
也许吧。

653
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:08.520
You'd have to be close, right?
你得凑得很近才行，对吧？

654
00:27:08.620 --> 00:27:09.480
Like over his shoulder.
就像在他肩膀后面那种。

655
00:27:09.700 --> 00:27:10.000
Yeah.
对。

656
00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:16.560
But, I mean, probably what a headache for Veda, like keeping track of all that, and then it didn't even make it in.
不过，我是说，这对薇达来说得多头疼啊，还得留意所有这些，结果最后还没用上。

657
00:27:16.840 --> 00:27:22.300
I'll have you know, Angela, at 2 minutes 48 seconds, we had a fan catch from Flora K.
安吉拉，我得告诉你，在2分48秒的时候，我们收到了一位名叫芙萝拉·K的粉丝的发现。

658
00:27:22.800 --> 00:27:27.300
There is a blooming plant at reception.
前台有一盆开花的植物。

659
00:27:27.980 --> 00:27:28.460
Flora!
芙萝拉！

660
00:27:28.760 --> 00:27:29.640
Good catch!
好眼力！

661
00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:31.300
I knew it would make your heart happy, Angela.
我知道这会让你很高兴，安吉拉。

662
00:27:31.300 --> 00:27:32.380
I saw it too, Flora.
我也看到了，芙萝拉。

663
00:27:32.800 --> 00:27:36.580
You know, the last time we had a blooming plant at reception was Beach Games.
你知道，我们上次在前台看到开花的植物还是在《海滩运动会》那集。

664
00:27:37.040 --> 00:27:39.240
So you think this is connected to Pam?
所以你觉得这跟帕姆有关？

665
00:27:39.400 --> 00:27:40.820
Pam is going to have her moment here.
帕姆在这里要高光时刻了。

666
00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:42.460
She's going to have another moment.
她还会有另一个高光时刻。

667
00:27:42.780 --> 00:27:45.620
She's going to bloom again today, like in Beach Games.
她今天会再次绽放，就像在《海滩运动会》里那样。

668
00:27:45.740 --> 00:27:52.620
Now, I know we talked to Steve Ducharer, who told us that it was a coincidence that it was a blooming plant for Beach Games.
现在，我知道我们跟史蒂夫·迪沙雷聊过，他告诉我们《海滩运动会》里出现开花的植物纯属巧合。

669
00:27:53.260 --> 00:27:58.060
But Steve Ducharer, again, with the blooming plant, Pam is blooming.
但史蒂夫·迪沙雷，又是开花的植物，帕姆正在绽放。

670
00:27:58.340 --> 00:27:59.440
I think it was subconscious.
我觉得这是潜意识的。

671
00:27:59.660 --> 00:28:00.820
This is that group mind thing.
这就是那种群体思维的事。

672
00:28:00.820 --> 00:28:01.660
That's what I was going to say.
这也是我正要说的。

673
00:28:01.740 --> 00:28:02.940
This is creative group mind.
这是创造性的群体思维。

674
00:28:03.360 --> 00:28:06.480
Well, Michael is now going to move into the kitchen.
好了，迈克尔现在要走进厨房了。

675
00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:07.680
I guess he's hungry.
我猜他饿了。

676
00:28:08.060 --> 00:28:09.660
So he's looking for some food.
所以他在找吃的。

677
00:28:10.160 --> 00:28:14.020
He's a little tipsy, and he's going to go, like, raid the refrigerator.
他有点喝醉了，打算去洗劫冰箱。

678
00:28:14.280 --> 00:28:15.260
Who hasn't been there?
谁没经历过这事呢？

679
00:28:15.340 --> 00:28:15.780
Come on.
得了吧。

680
00:28:16.380 --> 00:28:22.000
In the script, it just said that Michael takes out a container clearly labeled Phyllis.
剧本里只写着迈克尔拿出一个明显贴有菲莉丝标签的容器。

681
00:28:22.280 --> 00:28:25.340
But you know how he's eating it, and then he's like, ugh, Phyllis.
但你知道他是怎么吃的，然后他就一副“呃，菲莉丝”的表情。

682
00:28:25.560 --> 00:28:26.700
None of that was in the script.
这些在剧本里全都没有。

683
00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:28.120
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

684
00:28:28.460 --> 00:28:28.720
Nope.
没有。

685
00:28:28.960 --> 00:28:30.020
Steve just improvised that.
那是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

686
00:28:30.200 --> 00:28:31.640
Oh, that's so good.
哦，那太棒了。

687
00:28:32.220 --> 00:28:36.280
Andy comes in, and he wants to give Michael some wine as a farewell gift.
安迪进来了，他想送迈克尔一些酒作为告别礼物。

688
00:28:36.520 --> 00:28:38.660
It's actually a really nice gesture.
这其实是一个非常暖心的举动。

689
00:28:38.980 --> 00:28:39.860
It is.
确实是。

690
00:28:40.020 --> 00:28:42.380
And Michael just doesn't give a crap.
而迈克尔根本不在乎。

691
00:28:42.380 --> 00:28:45.960
Michael would love it if Jim came in and gave him a bottle of wine.
要是吉姆进来送他一瓶酒，迈克尔可会喜欢死了。

692
00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:46.760
I know.
我知道。

693
00:28:47.860 --> 00:28:51.380
But, you know, it's Andy, so he's like, ugh, I already have wine.
但你知道的，那是安迪，所以他就觉得，呃，我已经有酒了。

694
00:28:51.560 --> 00:28:57.520
This next scene I loved because Michael's sitting on the couch by front reception, and a man walks in.
我超喜欢接下来这场戏，因为迈克尔坐在前台旁边的沙发上，然后有个男人走了进来。

695
00:28:57.820 --> 00:29:00.600
He's interviewing for Michael's job.
他在面试迈克尔的工作。

696
00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:04.000
Yeah, Michael is kind of on the couch reading a novel.
对，迈克尔有点像在沙发上看小说。

697
00:29:04.300 --> 00:29:05.500
I zoomed in on it.
我把镜头拉近了。

698
00:29:05.680 --> 00:29:07.080
I tried to see what it was.
我试图看清那是什么书。

699
00:29:07.220 --> 00:29:09.400
It's like a woman in a martini glass.
封面好像是一个坐在马提尼酒杯里的女人。

700
00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:09.500
Yes.
没错。

701
00:29:10.220 --> 00:29:12.140
It's clearly like a sort of—
这显然有点像一种——

702
00:29:12.140 --> 00:29:12.720
A romance novel?
言情小说？

703
00:29:12.900 --> 00:29:20.840
No, it seems like one of those, like, books for women about, you know, claim your space sort of book.
不，感觉像是那种，你知道的，写给女性的关于“活出自我”之类的书。

704
00:29:20.980 --> 00:29:22.380
Yeah, yeah, like a motivational—
对，对，就像一本励志——

705
00:29:22.380 --> 00:29:23.000
Yes.
没错。

706
00:29:23.200 --> 00:29:24.600
That's what it looked like to me.
我看起来也是这样。

707
00:29:25.160 --> 00:29:27.020
I want you to know a couple of things.
我想让你知道几件事。

708
00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:30.840
At 4 minutes 16 seconds, the blooming plant is on the move.
在4分16秒时，那盆开花的植物动了。

709
00:29:30.980 --> 00:29:33.640
It's been moved to the other side of the reception desk.
它被移到了接待台的另一边。

710
00:29:33.800 --> 00:29:35.080
So you can see the couch better.
这样你们能看得更清楚沙发。

711
00:29:35.080 --> 00:29:45.580
The man who's interviewing for the job is named Mr. Isaac Sylvie, and Aaron Schur told us that he was named after Aaron's kids, Isaac and Sylvie.
那个来面试的人叫艾萨克·西尔维先生（Mr. Isaac Sylvie），亚伦·舒尔（Aaron Schur）告诉我们，这个名字是用亚伦的孩子艾萨克和西尔维的名字命名的。

712
00:29:45.760 --> 00:29:46.720
Isn't that so cute?
这不是很可爱吗？

713
00:29:46.860 --> 00:29:47.260
Yes!
对啊！

714
00:29:47.540 --> 00:29:55.380
He had originally named the character Mr. Engbritsen, but Paul Lieberstein told him, no, name him after your kids.
他原本给这个角色取名叫恩格布里森先生（Mr. Engbritsen），但保罗·利伯斯坦（Paul Lieberstein）告诉他，不行，用你孩子名字命名。

715
00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:58.560
So that's how he got the name Mr. Isaac Sylvie.
所以他就得到了艾萨克·西尔维先生这个名字。

716
00:29:58.560 --> 00:30:07.980
He was played by David Grant Wright, who has appeared in several episodes of Better Call Saul, Crazy Ex-Girlfriend, and Brooklyn Nine-Nine,
他由大卫·格兰特·赖特（David Grant Wright）饰演，他曾在《风骚律师》、《疯狂前女友》和《神烦警探》的多集里出现过，

717
00:30:08.100 --> 00:30:10.680
and pretty much every soap opera you can imagine.
几乎演过你能想象到的每一部肥皂剧。

718
00:30:10.940 --> 00:30:15.200
David is an incredible actor, and I read his bio.
大卫是个了不起的演员，我读过他的简历。

719
00:30:15.540 --> 00:30:18.140
He is a 27-year cancer survivor.
他是战胜癌症27年的幸存者。

720
00:30:18.400 --> 00:30:19.180
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

721
00:30:19.180 --> 00:30:30.120
He wrote a one-man show called With Flying Colors about his cancer experience, which he has performed for the last 25 years, raising thousands of dollars for cancer patients.
他写了一部名为《凯旋而归》（With Flying Colors）的独角戏，讲述了他抗癌的经历，并在过去25年里一直坚持表演，为癌症患者筹集了数千美元。

722
00:30:30.700 --> 00:30:31.800
Good human alert.
好人警报。

723
00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:32.440
Yes.
对。

724
00:30:32.680 --> 00:30:33.300
Good human alert.
好人警报。

725
00:30:33.540 --> 00:30:34.100
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

726
00:30:34.540 --> 00:30:40.100
Well, in this scene, Michael finds out that Isaac has driven all the way from Philly.
在这场戏里，迈克尔发现艾萨克是从费城一路开车过来的。

727
00:30:40.300 --> 00:30:42.760
Michael's like, gosh, that's a heck of a drive.
迈克尔就说，天哪，这可真是好长一段车程。

728
00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:45.880
And Isaac said, yeah, well, this is one of the few places hiring.
艾萨克说，是啊，不过这也是少数几个还在招人的地方了。

729
00:30:46.080 --> 00:30:47.320
It's rough out there.
现在外面不好混啊。

730
00:30:47.320 --> 00:30:50.800
And you sort of see the realization coming over Michael's face.
然后你能看到迈克尔脸上露出了恍然大悟的表情。

731
00:30:51.260 --> 00:30:52.640
Jenna, there was more to the scene.
珍娜，这场戏其实还有更多内容。

732
00:30:52.740 --> 00:30:53.840
And it was so good.
而且非常精彩。

733
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:55.260
I read it in the shooting draft.
我在拍摄剧本里读到了。

734
00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:57.900
He has his resume out, Isaac.
艾萨克拿出了他的简历。

735
00:30:58.060 --> 00:30:59.300
And Michael's like, can I see that?
迈克尔就说，我能看看吗？

736
00:30:59.680 --> 00:31:01.060
Michael is so blown away.
迈克尔大受震撼。

737
00:31:01.200 --> 00:31:05.320
He finds out that Isaac was the president of the company he used to work at.
他发现艾萨克曾是他以前工作那家公司的总裁。

738
00:31:05.900 --> 00:31:06.340
Wow.
哇。

739
00:31:06.640 --> 00:31:07.040
Yeah.
是啊。

740
00:31:07.240 --> 00:31:10.960
And now he's driving all the way from Philly for a regional manager position.
而现在他为了一个地区经理的职位，从费城一路开车过来。

741
00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:13.340
Michael is so blown away by his resume.
迈克尔被他的简历深深地震撼了。

742
00:31:13.520 --> 00:31:14.920
He says, can I keep this?
他说，这个我可以留着吗？

743
00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:18.160
And then he really starts to spiral.
然后他真的开始情绪失控了。

744
00:31:18.420 --> 00:31:25.180
And he goes to see Toby and asks Toby for resume advice, like how to beef up his resume.
他去找托比，向托比征求关于简历的建议，比如怎么把简历写得更丰富。

745
00:31:25.660 --> 00:31:27.640
This made it into the deleted scenes.
这段被剪进删减片段里了。

746
00:31:27.840 --> 00:31:28.520
It's so good.
非常精彩。

747
00:31:28.700 --> 00:31:29.360
Can we hear it?
我们能听听吗？

748
00:31:30.180 --> 00:31:32.300
Hey, Toby, I have a real quick question for you.
嘿，托比，我有个很小的问题想问你。

749
00:31:32.460 --> 00:31:33.540
It's about a resume.
关于一份简历的。

750
00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:34.200
Sure.
当然可以。

751
00:31:34.540 --> 00:31:39.980
So we might start with, so your most recent thing, you know, summary of achievements.
所以我们可以从这里开始，也就是你最近的事迹，你知道的，成就总结。

752
00:31:39.980 --> 00:31:41.780
What have you done here at Dunder Mifflin?
你在这里邓德米夫林都做过什么？

753
00:31:43.080 --> 00:31:44.740
Regional manager, Dick Watt.
区域经理，迪克·瓦特。

754
00:31:44.840 --> 00:31:45.600
Okay, what's your title?
好吧，你的头衔是什么？

755
00:31:45.880 --> 00:31:49.520
You know, how would you actually describe what you did?
你知道的，你到底会怎么描述你做过的事？

756
00:31:49.920 --> 00:31:50.840
Changed things.
改变了现状。

757
00:31:51.080 --> 00:31:55.580
Ushered in a new era of love and comedy in the workplace.
开启了职场爱与喜剧的新时代。

758
00:31:57.180 --> 00:31:58.160
Hired many.
雇用了许多人。

759
00:31:58.420 --> 00:31:59.280
Fired none.
解雇了零个人。

760
00:32:00.180 --> 00:32:01.080
Made money.
赚了钱。

761
00:32:01.720 --> 00:32:02.400
Lost money.
赔了钱。

762
00:32:03.560 --> 00:32:04.780
Learned to stop counting.
学会了不再去数。

763
00:32:08.040 --> 00:32:09.180
This is our moment.
这是我们的时刻。

764
00:32:11.320 --> 00:32:12.120
This is our time.
这是我们的时代。

765
00:32:15.200 --> 00:32:17.480
This next part should be sung, if possible.
接下来的这部分如果可以的话应该唱出来。

766
00:32:18.200 --> 00:32:19.780
That made me laugh so hard.
那把我笑得不行。

767
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:21.200
The scene continued.
镜头继续。

768
00:32:21.780 --> 00:32:24.600
Toby said, how would you describe what you did?
托比说，你将如何描述你所做的事？

769
00:32:24.880 --> 00:32:26.700
And Michael has this speech.
然后迈克尔有这样一段演讲。

770
00:32:26.840 --> 00:32:28.040
And it didn't make it in.
结果没被剪进去。

771
00:32:28.540 --> 00:32:30.480
This is Michael talking about himself.
这是迈克尔在谈论他自己。

772
00:32:31.100 --> 00:32:34.800
Michael Scott always had a strange recipe for success.
迈克尔·斯科特总有一套奇怪的成功秘诀。

773
00:32:35.060 --> 00:32:36.360
Two cups of spirit.
两杯激情。

774
00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:38.360
A half a thing of inspiration.
半份灵感。

775
00:32:38.740 --> 00:32:40.320
Two spoonfuls of love.
两勺爱。

776
00:32:40.320 --> 00:32:41.920
A water bottle of danger.
一水瓶危险。

777
00:32:42.220 --> 00:32:43.280
A pinch of praise.
一小撮赞美。

778
00:32:43.400 --> 00:32:44.260
A dash of hopes.
少许希望。

779
00:32:44.400 --> 00:32:45.380
A sprinkle of cinnamon.
一把肉桂粉。

780
00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:46.960
Two pats of butter.
两小块黄油。

781
00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:48.520
A box of cake mix.
一盒蛋糕预拌粉。

782
00:32:48.640 --> 00:32:50.040
And a little bit of cooking oil.
以及一点点食用油。

783
00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:51.360
Preheat of it.
预热一下。

784
